**Sport Science Symposium** — 8 talks Eric attended/recorded solo on **2026-05-30** (Fireflies, `*_SportSciSympo`). Reference material for R&D, essays, and the [[practice-load-framework]] / OKR work.

**Talks & themes:**
- **Patrick Ward** — research/publishing in applied sport science.
- **Panel: Data Architecture** (John Wagle, Cam, JW — `JN-CM-JW_PanelDataArchitecture`) — internal "listening tours" to understand existing data measures + their rationale; eliminate unreliable/inefficient collection; strict data-communication + viz standards; choose tech by **industry norms, not individual staff preference** (scalability).
- **Kate Weiss** — **ADI metrics** (mechanical work subcategories, mechanical power, acceleration profiles); push toward a **drill-level ADI metric** + time-based mechanical-power intensity zones; report mechanical work/power to coaches across comparable training days.
- **Adam Parr** — (sport-science application).
- **Sam Contorno** — training volume + **periodization** (Stanford & Texas models); **backward planning from game-week volume**; protect player availability across the season.
- **Duncan French** — sport science as methodology; bioenergetics; advanced + sport-specific testing (horizontal sled, boxing tests); **NIRS** + respiratory/cardiac/metabolic athlete profiling; role of AI in conditioning.
- **Cam Josse** — data validity + tool confidence; **graded explanations / clear coding systems**; manage **cognitive load** when presenting data to coaches/players (concise, actionable).
- **Nick Winkelman** — Irish Rugby's leadership + data practices; **co-authorship culture**; national dosing standards for sprint/speed exposure; centralized health/performance dashboards with provincial data anonymity; instrumented mouthguards.
- Also surfaced (**Dan Joss**): purposeful evidence-based data systems; standardized biomech-interpretation frameworks; **multivariate convergence + mixed-effects models** to flag individual deviation; **Bayesian** comms over p-values.

Recurring threads: data validity/communication, periodization from game-week backward, mechanical-load (ADI) granularity, AI in performance, governance/standards.
